                <mxCell id="n1" value="The only entry point that pulls pixels&#xa;&#xa;render() pulls them later, while slicing; layoutPagesFromHeaders()&#xa;never pulls any. Here the whole point is the copy-out, so the cost&#xa;is a full decode and scale of one page.&#xa;&#xa;The caller allocates and owns rgba — no allocation crosses the&#xa;library boundary. A size mismatch throws rather than writing a&#xa;plausible-looking wrong image, so a stale layout surfaces at once." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="490" y="950" width="390" height="150" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="n2" value="Why the result is always RGBA8888&#xa;&#xa;sRGB is 8-bit by definition in libvips, so the colourspace call&#xa;settles both space and depth; addalpha then fixes the band count.&#xa;Both are no-ops for a page that already is 8-bit sRGB RGBA.&#xa;&#xa;The narrowing is for the caller&#39;s convenience — the committed&#xa;render still keeps the source&#39;s own format." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="490" y="1110" width="390" height="130" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
